[line]
[size=4][b][color=#42ACC8]Actual Gear, Registered Appearance Visibility, and Conditions[/color][/b][/size]


Hiding actual gear is visual only and does not unequip it or remove its armor rating, enchantments, or effects. Hiding a registered appearance removes only its display and preserves registration.

Global hide and per-item eye controls compose normally. If individual items differ from the global state, the global checkbox shows the correct partial state. Automatic external-mod state follows the same display rule.

Conditional appearances take priority over the same actor's base appearance. Condition and action cards are preserved independently, and empty condition/action areas share the same drag-and-drop behavior and visual style.

[line]
[size=4][b][color=#42ACC8]Actors and NPCs[/color][/b][/size]


Registered appearances, actual-gear hiding, conditions, external transactions, and temporary display state are actor-local. The actor selector lists the player, NPCs with saved data, and currently nearby NPCs. Hostile actors and corpses are excluded from automatic nearby detection.

Although every actor uses the same policy and mapping table, actual results are stored only for the affected FormID. A SexLab scene or wardrobe replacement involving NPC A cannot change NPC B or the player.

[line]
[size=4][b][color=#42ACC8]Protected Special-Effect Slots and Shields[/color][/b][/size]


Slots 50, 51, 60, and 61 are protected by default and can be customized across slots 30–61.

[list]
[*]Actual gear containing a protected slot always remains visible[/*]
[*]New appearance registration for protected items is blocked[/*]
[*]Existing base and conditional appearances stay inactive while protected and return when protection is removed[/*]
[*]Equipment, Outfit, Kit, condition registration, and the strip-link popup use the same filter[/*]
[/list]


[b]Use Shields as Appearance Slots[/b] is OFF by default. When off, the actual slot-39 shield remains visible and shield appearance registration is blocked. When enabled, slot 39 works as an ordinary appearance slot.

[line]
[size=4][b][color=#42ACC8]Fitting Kits[/color][/b][/size]


Virtual game path:

[font=Courier New]Data/Interface/SkyrimFittingSystem/user/kits[/font]

Inside the SFS MO2 mod folder, do not create another [font=Courier New]Data[/font] directory. Use:

[font=Courier New]Interface/SkyrimFittingSystem/user/kits[/font]

The built-in [b]Kit Generator[/b] writes finished JSON files directly here. Externally created kits can also be copied into this folder. UTF-8 Korean, Chinese, other Unicode names and paths, and UTF-8 BOM files are supported; invalid or unreadable JSON is skipped safely.

[line]
[size=4][b][color=#42ACC8]RaceMenu BodyMorph and Wig Color[/color][/b][/size]


When RaceMenu is present, SFS follows RaceMenu's common BodyMorph/NiOverride update path instead of a list of mod-specific events. There is no polling or global actor scan; only the actor receiving a real morph update and that actor's active registered appearance nodes are processed across DAVE, DAV, and native paths.

If registered wigs become darker after loading a save, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/156414]Hair Colour Sync NG[/url] is recommended. Use [font=Courier New]bEnableTintHairSlot=0[/font] in RaceMenu's [font=Courier New]Data/SKSE/Plugins/skee64.ini[/font] and do not combine multiple wig-color synchronization mods.

[line]
[size=4][b][color=#42ACC8]SOS / TNG and Naked-State Checks[/color][/b][/size]


SFS evaluates the final visible combination of actual gear and registered appearances. Original-mod and user-assigned revealing or concealing policy has priority, while SFS-owned runtime keywords are tracked and cleaned safely.

Automatic slot-32/49 classification minimizes source-ARMO mutation. A confirmed slot-32 upper-only item removes opposite SFS-owned Concealing/Covering state and gains Revealing keywords. Ordinary full-body slot-32 armor already conceals through normal SOS/TNG slot behavior, so SFS clears only conflicting SFS Revealing state and does not add Concealing, Covering, or Underwear keywords. A classified slot-49 lower garment gains Concealing/Covering and Underwear keywords because basic SOS/TNG behavior may not conceal slot 49 automatically. Keywords originally supplied by an ESP, KID, or another mod are never deleted.

The slot-32 upper-only name classifier ignores generic vanilla equipment taxonomy such as [font=Courier New]ArmorCuirass[/font], [font=Courier New]ArmorHeavy[/font], [font=Courier New]ArmorLight[/font], [font=Courier New]ArmorMaterial*[/font], [font=Courier New]ClothingBody[/font], and [font=Courier New]VendorItemArmor[/font]. Item names, EditorIDs, and semantic mod/KID keywords remain available, preventing ordinary vanilla armor from being mistaken for a [font=Courier New]top[/font], [font=Courier New]bra[/font], or [font=Courier New]shirt[/font].

Papyrus and Skyrim engine-condition [font=Courier New]WornHasKeyword[/font] checks use the same actor-local final body display state. The actor is covered when either actual slot-32 gear or a registered slot-32 appearance is displayed, and uncovered when both are hidden. This does not forcibly replace the private logic of an external DLL that scans inventory directly.

[line]
[size=4][b][color=#42ACC8]DAV / DAVE / Native Environments[/color][/b][/size]


SFS separates DAVE's public refresh API, ordinary DAV follow-up, and Skyrim-native skinning. Save format, actor ownership, registered FormIDs, and original slots remain identical across environments.

[line]
[size=4][b][color=#42ACC8]Wet Function Redux[/color][/b][/size]


Wet Function Redux applies wet effects to SFS registered appearances through the separate optional compatibility patch.

[line]
[size=4][b][color=#42ACC8]Built-in Helmet Toggle 2 Integration[/color][/b][/size]


Helmet Toggle 2 needs no separate SFS patch. SFSCore observes only HT2's exact player state global and exact actor-local NPC/follower spell transitions. It reads the managed real ARMO's full slots, excludes pure registered slot 31, and lets registered 31+42 cards follow through slot 42. When a hidden, still-equipped real headgear occupies Hair 31, SFS releases only that actor's Hair bit from the renderer's worn mask so the original hair is skinned. There is no periodic actor scan, and SFS never edits HT2 scripts, calls, actual equipment, DAVE variants, or Mod-Configured virtual tokens.

[line]
[size=4][b][color=#42ACC8]Optional Compatibility Patches[/color][/b][/size]


[list]
[*][b]Dynamic Feminine Female Modesty Animations OAR 4.30:[/b] the separate FOMOD changes only its selected OAR JSON conditions to read SFS's final displayed outfit. It does not replace DFFMA animations, meshes, scripts, DLLs, or plugins.[/*]
[*][b]Wet Function Redux Visual Effect Patch v1.2.0:[/b] supplies only the visual-effect script. It never replaces Wet Function's MCM script; a RaceMenu warning is Wet Function's own legacy self-check, not an SFS equipment or save-data modification.[/*]
[*][b]Dynamic Footprints SKSE BASE v3:[/b] the separate patch reads only a visible SFS Feet 37 appearance for Dynamic Footprints' own footprint classification and otherwise uses actual footwear. It disables itself unless the exact verified v3 DLL build is present.[/*]
[/list]


[line]
[size=4][b][color=#42ACC8]External Runtime Menu API[/color][/b][/size]


The API module name changed from [font=Courier New]SkyrimFittingSystem.dll[/font] to [font=Courier New]SFSCore.dll[/font] in v1.4.0. External shortcut and menu-management mods must therefore look up [font=Courier New]SFSCore.dll[/font] when resolving these functions:

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]SkyrimFittingSystem_Open[/font][/*]
[*][font=Courier New]SkyrimFittingSystem_Close[/font][/*]
[*][font=Courier New]SkyrimFittingSystem_IsMenuOpen[/font][/*]
[*][font=Courier New]SkyrimFittingSystem_SetHotkeyEnabled[/font][/*]
[/list]


Only the DLL lookup name changed. The four C export names and function signatures remain unchanged. Consumers supporting both versions should try [font=Courier New]SFSCore.dll[/font] first, then fall back to [font=Courier New]SkyrimFittingSystem.dll[/font] for v1.3.x. Requests are transferred to SFS's safe UI processing point, and hotkey enable state resets on every game launch. An updated consumer header and [font=Courier New]GetProcAddress[/font] example are included in the source package.

